    "actual_bases": null,
    "why_iomem_is_insufficient": "Both are mapped 4 KiB reservations without no-map. Reserved RAM may still appear under System RAM, and current iomem has no separate labels for these reservations.",
    "why_callback_logs_are_missing": "The mt6885 legacy DRAMC callbacks print addresses, but their Makefile is gated by CONFIG_MTK_DRAMC/CONFIG_MTK_DRAMC_WA; both are disabled. The running config instead enables CONFIG_MEDIATEK_DRAMC. The generic OF allocator still allocates size nodes regardless of a compatible callback.",
